+# Judiciary independent disposition — `executive_unhealthy:1795562202`
+
+Inspected 2026-11-24T23:36Z–23:38Z. Office: independent Viche Judiciary (Act 4), accountable to
+Parliament and the Founder, not to the Executive or Clerk. Fact-finding and measurement only: no
+law, ballot, corrective-case state, gate, audit algorithm, correction trail or Founder-owned file
+was changed. No reform is proposed, sponsored, ratified or implemented.
+
+## 1. The mandatory cross-branch case (verbatim from the dispatch)
+
+`executive_unhealthy:1795562202` — signal `executive_unhealthy`; owner `executive`; `state: open`;
+`first_seen` 1795562202 (23:16:42Z); `last_seen` 1795562442 (23:20:42Z); `observations` 4;
+`clear_observations` 19; `last_clear_observed_at` 1795563351 (23:35:51Z). Closure rule: automatic
+after 20 consecutive clear observations, or earlier by a Clerk record of an independent Judiciary
+disposition. These are health observations, not verdicts or legislative authorizations.
+
+## 2. What the signal actually is (read from code, not inferred from the label)
+
+`government/branch-health.sh` emits `<branch>_unhealthy` only when `state/branches/<branch>.json`
+is fresh (within `max_age`, default 1800 s), structurally valid, and carries `readiness ==
+"unhealthy"`. `branch-liveness.sh` writes that value when the branch cycle was not accepted, the
+agent status was unreadable after bounded re-probes, or the agent state fell outside
+`running|idle|clearexit`. It is a **branch-readiness observation**, not a finding about delivered
+work; the branch file itself carries `caveat: "readiness_not_proof_of_agent_progress_or_completed_work"`.
+
